! Make a local copy of the CDMS catalogue for WEEDS (run once: class -nw @tools/make_catalog.class).
! The range below (210-265 GHz) covers the examples. For your data, edit the output name and the
! frequency range [MHz] so that it covers all your spectra, and set  catalog: <that file>  in the config.
! For JPL use "use in jpl" (JPL species names have no ", v=0", e.g. SO instead of 'SO, v=0').
! CDMS species names contain spaces/commas (e.g. 'SO, v=0'); mcWEEDS quotes them for WEEDS.
use in cdms
use out data/cdms_210_265_GHz.db
select /freq 210000 265000
insert
exit
